    "expressible": false,
    "how": "every reachable (cart, pressed, latched) transition of `lp-iface-comb2`, `lp-iface-comb3`, `lp-iface-comb4`, `lp-iface-comb5`, `atrium` was enumerated under a 200000-state bound that raises rather than truncating, and each transition's occupancy-vector delta was summed. The cart's one-hot contributes 0 whether it moves or is blocked; latch bits and `pressed` are monotone and at most one turns on per transition (both checked in the loop, not assumed), so the sum is the number of bits that turned on. Measured sums [0, 1], none of them -1, against lp_potential's invariant -1. The shipped comb_open(.., 20, ..) was NOT enumerated -- 40 latch bits, ~4.4e13 states, which is the impossibility this ticket is about; the step from these levels to every size is the monotonicity argument above, supported by the corridor-length sweep (4x the latch bits, identical sums and kinds), not by a sweep of the shipped size.",
